35
00:01:34.359 --> 00:01:35.685
Thermometer!

36
00:01:35.985 --> 00:01:36.870
Excellent!

37
00:01:37.883 --> 00:01:46.416
Cough, Cough, Cough! Fever, Fever, Fever! Headache, Headache, Headache! Tummy ache, Tummy ache!

38
00:01:46.716 --> 00:01:56.966
Sore throat, Sore throat! Runny nose, Runny nose! Bandage, Bandage, Bandage! Thermometer, Thermometer, Thermometer!

39
00:01:57.266 --> 00:01:60.000
Clap, clap! Great chanting!

40
00:02:00.983 --> 00:02:12.499
Malis does not feel well. She has a cough and a runny nose. Mom uses a thermometer, and Malis has a fever. She drinks water, rests in bed and feels better soon.

41
00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.031
I love this story, Ms. Lily!

42
00:02:16.017 --> 00:02:18.228
What is it? Can you say it?

43
00:02:21.128 --> 00:02:22.991
Cough! Well done!

44
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:26.392
What is it? Can you say it?

45
00:02:29.292 --> 00:02:31.387
Fever! Well done!

46
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:34.641
What is it? Can you say it?

47
00:02:37.541 --> 00:02:40.309
Tummy ache! Well done!

48
00:02:41.317 --> 00:02:42.759
Let's say it together!

49
00:02:43.059 --> 00:02:45.816
I have a headache. I have a sore throat.

50
00:02:46.616 --> 00:02:47.756
Your turn!

51
00:02:51.256 --> 00:02:54.106
I have a headache. I have a sore throat.

52
00:02:55.117 --> 00:02:57.000
What do you do when you feel sick?

53
00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.568
I have a headache.

54
00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:02.962
Great answer!

55
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.948
Today's value is self-care. Look after yourself and rest when you are sick.

56
00:03:09.248 --> 00:03:11.050
I will try, Ms. Lily!

57
00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:17.271
Great job today, everyone! See you in Unit fifteen. Bye-bye!

58
00:03:17.571 --> 00:03:19.466
Bye-bye!

